Tools for Analysts (10 mins)
A key part of protecting an organization from threats is having the right security controls and investigation tools in place. 

1. SIEM
The SOC uses Splunk Enterprise Security (ES) as its SIEM to support event analysis, integration of threat intelligence, and detection of threats.

2. AUTOMATION
The SOC uses Splunk SOAR to automatically run mitigations when suspicious activities are detected. Splunk SOAR is a security orchestration, automation, and response (SOAR) platform.
It supports playbooks, which are sequences of actions and decision points that can run automatically and that help guide incident response.

3. TRAFFIC ANALYSIS
in the Wonderland SOC we use Wireshark and tcpdump to analyze network traffic. 
Both of these tools are open source and allow you to capture and save network traffic, or analyze it using various filters. 
Tcpdump is a command-line tool built for Unix-like systems, whereas Wireshark provides a GUI interface. Wireshark does offer a command-line-only version called TShark which is similar to tcpdump, and can be used on Windows or Unix-like systems.

4. CYBERSWISS ARMY KNIFE
In Wonderland, our analysts often use CyberChef from within a web browser to analyze or manipulate data. 
This tool can carry out various operations such as simple encoding like Base64, more complex encryption like AES, DES, or Blowfish, creating binary and hex dumps, compression and decompression of data, calculation of hashes and checksums, parsing data, and much more.


